al GDP growth by 0.8 percentage points by the end of 2020. Evaluate the likely impact of an increase in protectionism on the global economy.","topics":["4-1-6-restrictions-on-free-trade"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-4"],"keywords":["protectionism","tariffs","trade war","China","United States"],"qpPage":29,"msPage":20,"ctxPage":null,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"edexcel-a-p2-2021-nov-q6d","p":16,"section":"B","questionNumber":"6(d)","parentQuestion":"6","choiceGroup":null,"marks":12,"questionText":"Discuss the likely impact on Rwandan consumers and clothing manufacturers of the increase in the tariff on imports of second-hand clothes. Use an appropriate diagram to support your answer.","topics":["4-1-6-restrictions-on-free-trade"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-4"],"keywords":["tariff","imports","protectionism","Rwanda","diagram"],"qpPage":16,"msPage":14,"ctxPage":14,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"edexcel-a-p2-2018-jun-q1a","p":10,"section":"A","questionNumber":"1(a)","parentQuestion":"1","choiceGroup":null,"marks":1,"questionText":"The trade deal known as the Comprehensive Economic and Trade Agreement (CETA) is designed to eliminate or reduce trade barriers between the European Union (EU) and Canada. It is estimated that it will increase trade by 20% and boost EU GDP by 12 billion euros. Which one of the following is most likely to decrease as a result of CETA?","topics":["4-1-5-trading-blocs-and-the-world-trade-organisation","4-1-6-restrictions-on-free-trade"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-4"],"keywords":["trade agreement","CETA","tariffs"],"qpPage":2,"msPage":4,"ctxPage":null,"modelAnswer":null,"type":"mcq","options":["Economic growth in EU countries","Exports from EU countries to Canada","Imports from Canada to EU countries","Tariffs on European exports to Canada"],"usesFigure":false},{"id":"edexcel-a-p2-2017-jun-q7","p":9,"section":"C","questionNumber":"7","parentQuestion":null,"choiceGroup":"edexcel-a-p2-2017-jun-sec-c","marks":25,"questionText":"Since the global financial crisis of 2008 there have been over 5 700 increases in tariffs, quotas and administrative controls on international trade. Evaluate the likely effects of an increase in protectionism on the economy of a developing country of your choice.","topics":["4-1-6-restrictions-on-free-trade"],"board":"edexcel","groups":["theme-4"],"keywords":["protectionism","tariffs","quotas","developing countries","trade barriers"],"qpPage":29,"msPage":18,"ctxPage":null,"modelAnswer":null}]}
